          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Trairasika—The Rule of Three"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.571,
            0.848,
            0.647
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 8:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " For the mid-day meal in a school with 120 students, the cook usually makes 15 kg of rice. On a rainy day, only 80 students came to school. How many kilograms of rice should the cook make so that the food is not wasted?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.65,
            0.847,
            0.69
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The ratio of the number of students to the amount of rice needs to be proportional."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.406,
            0.687,
            0.593,
            0.708
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_8_equation_16.jpg",
          "content": "\\S 0 , 1 2 0 : 1 5 : : 8 0 : ?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.714,
            0.598,
            0.738
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "What is the factor of change in the first term?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.738,
            0.598,
            0.766
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We can find that by dividing the terms "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "{ \\frac { 8 0 } { 1 2 0 } } = { \\frac { 2 } { 3 } } ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.766,
            0.65,
            0.791
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The number of students is reduced by a factor of "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 2 } { 3 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.793,
            0.763,
            0.814
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "On multiplying the weight of rice by the same factor, we get,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 21,
          "bbox": [
            0.457,
            0.816,
            0.565,
            0.842
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_8_equation_21.jpg",
          "content": "1 5 \\times { \\frac { 2 } { 3 } } = 1 0 ."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 22,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.844,
            0.641,
            0.865
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "So, the cook should make 10 kg of rice on that day."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 23,
          "bbox": [
